BEGIN_DESC
AtmoFX alpha, level 1 (stock D3D9 client). Automatic descent: the probe starts 620 km above Jupiter's reference radius - over the stock cloud layer (480 km) - and sinks at 1 km/s to 448 km, drifting north at 0.5 km/s. Under the stock layer (now a ceiling) the AtmoFX decks, cumulus impostors and lightning under the deck appear.
Keys: K - AtmoFX clouds on/off (before/after, FPS). J - lightning on/off. Numpad8/2 - climb/descend (stops the descent, Shift x10). Numpad4/6 - drift slower/faster, Numpad5 - stop. Time acceleration speeds up the descent and the drift. Ctrl+arrows / right mouse button - look around.
END_DESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 60970.5
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship Probe
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET Probe
  MODE Cockpit
  FOV 55.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Surface
END_HUD

BEGIN_SHIPS
Probe:AtmoProbe
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 0.00
  TOUR 620 448 1.0
  DRIFT 0.5
  SUNELEV 30
END
END_SHIPS
